{"name":"Wood Lake","hex":"#a08475","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance making up the central part of the trunk and branches of a tree. Used as a material for construction, to manufacture various items, etc. or as fuel.","The wood from a particular species of tree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or plant with trees.","To hide behind trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood"},{"term":"lake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, landlocked stretch of water or similar liquid.","A large amount of liquid."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An offering, sacrifice, gift.","Play; sport; game; fun; glee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wood Lake, Louisiana","blocks":[{"text":"Wood Lake is an Isleño fishing community in St. Bernard Parish, Louisiana, United States. The community is situated along Bayou Terre-aux-Boeufs to the northeast of Delacroix, Louisiana and west of Lake Lery. Following the American Civil War, the community was founded by Isleño hunters, trappers, and fisherman."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Wood_Lake%2C_Louisiana.jpg/330px-Wood_Lake%2C_Louisiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood_Lake%2C_Louisiana"},{"title":"Wood Lake, Minnesota","blocks":[{"text":"Wood Lake is a city in Yellow Medicine County, Minnesota, United States. The population was 381 at the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Yellow_Medicine_County_Minnesota_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Wood_Lake_Highlighted.svg/330px-Yellow_Medicine_County_Minnesota_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Wood_Lake_Highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood_Lake%2C_Minnesota"},{"title":"Wood Lake (British Columbia)","blocks":[{"text":"Wood Lake is a lake in a chain of five major lakes which occupies portions of the Okanagan Valley in the interior of British Columbia, Canada. \nThe lakes of the Okanagan Valley were formed by about 8900 BP.\nWood Lake is immediately south of Kalamalka Lake and in 1908 was connected to it by a dredged channel. \nSituated between Oyama and Winfield, it has a solid reputation for rainbow trout fishing. \nThe lake is named after Tom Wood, who settled on the south end of the lake around 1860."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Looking_Northward_along_the_West_Shoreline_of_Wood_Lake_BC_in_Summer.webm/330px--Looking_Northward_along_the_West_Shoreline_of_Wood_Lake_BC_in_Summer.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood_Lake_(British_Columbia)"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a natural, lignocellulosic material derived primarily from the secondary xylem of trees and other woody plants, where it provides mechanical support and in the functional sapwood, conducts water and dissolved minerals. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Trumpeters_by_Oyama_BC.jpg/120px-Trumpeters_by_Oyama_BC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Trumpeters_by_Oyama_BC.jpg/250px-Trumpeters_by_Oyama_BC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.